{"to":"C","text":"Thanks for getting in touch, C. I'm glad to help, and I want to be clear about what I am: a neutral helper who keeps track of everyone's concerns and helps you find a plan. I can't make legal decisions or move money for you.

I'll start a list of concerns from all three of you and share it with everyone, so you can all see it and disagree with it.

To begin, can you tell me two things? First, what do you want to end up with, in your own words? Second, what worries you most about A's idea of a family discount? For example, is your worry about the price, about being asked to sign something, or about how B is treated? If you have a copy of the will or know what it says about the house, send me the main points."}

{"to":"A","text":"Hello, A. My name is not important, but my role is: I'm a neutral helper the family has asked to sort out the house and the will. I don't make legal decisions and I can't move money. What I do is collect everyone's concerns, keep them on one list, and help you agree on a plan.

C has told me you and your husband would like to buy the house at what she called a family discount. I'd like to hear it from you directly. What are you hoping the purchase would look like, and what do you need it to include? What worries you about the situation?

I'll write down your concerns and share them with A, B and C so everyone can check them, and I'll expect the same of everyone else's."}

{"to":"B","text":"Hello, B. I'm a neutral helper the family has asked to help sort out the house and your father's will. I don't make legal decisions and I can't move money. My job is to gather each sister's concerns on one list and help you all reach a plan.

C tells me you could use some money from this. I'd like to hear your side directly. What would help you most, and what worries you? Do you want a share of the house's value paid out to you, or something else? And do you have any view on A buying the house?

I'll put your concerns on the shared list and send it to A, B and C, so please tell me if I get them wrong."}

